\use{document}
\use{chem}

\title{Reactions with \texttt{chem}}
\author{The texish project}
\maketitle

\section{Reaction equations}

Written in compact, mhchem-style notation with \texttt{\\ce}, a reaction is parsed
and set in math mode — element symbols upright, atom counts as subscripts,
coefficients at full size, and the operators and arrows as math symbols. The
combustion of methane is \texttt{\\ce\{CH4 + 2 O2 -> CO2 + 2 H2O\}}:

\bigskip
\centerline{\font lmroman 14 regular \ce{CH4 + 2 O2 -> CO2 + 2 H2O}}
\bigskip

\noindent The Haber process is reversible, with the equilibrium arrow
\texttt{<=>}:

\bigskip
\centerline{\font lmroman 14 regular \ce{N2 + 3 H2 <=> 2 NH3}}
\bigskip

\vfill\eject
